{
  "0": "Add a deterministic repeat-frequency feature by multiplying each nonpadding input item embedding by 1 + 0.1*log(1+c), where c counts that item's earlier occurrences within the available causal prefix. Compute counts identically during training and prediction, without future interactions. This may distinguish recurring interests from isolated purchases. Keep learned embeddings, SASRec topology, readout, loss and optimizer unchanged; train one model per category.",
  "1": "Replace each SASRec feed-forward sublayer's activation with GELU, preserving its widths, layer count, residual paths and attention configuration. Smoother activation may improve optimization of sparse interaction histories without increasing model size materially. Preserve features, embeddings, scoring, history selection, readout, loss and optimizer; train one model per category.",
  "2": "Index the existing positional embedding table by distance from the newest available interaction: newest=0, preceding=1, with padding masked. Preserve chronological token order, causal attention, context length and embedding-table dimensions. Consistent recency positions across different history lengths may improve next-item ranking. Keep all other features, SASRec topology, readout, loss and optimizer fixed; train one model per category.",
  "3": "Apply a learning-rate schedule to the baseline optimizer: linear warmup over the first 5% of training steps to the baseline learning rate, then cosine decay to 10% of that rate at the existing epoch cap, at most 200. Gradual warmup and late refinement may improve validation HR@10. Preserve model, features, loss, batch size, dropout, weight decay, seeds and checkpoint-selection rule; train one model per category."
}
